  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AMHQRM Enterprise Expansion Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Azimio is an expansion rice value chain project that has successfully implemented an USADF supported capacity building project. The expansion project is expected to benefit more than 800 smallholder rice farmers at the Azimio Mswiswi irrigation scheme. Through continued USADF grant and technical support the project seeks to complete the on-going construction of its own warehouse and offices on a newly acquired piece of land in Azimio Mswiswi Village. The group also needs to improve the quality of rice they process so as to remain a competitive rice processor and supplier. The group will need a delivery track to ensure members paddy once harvested is delivered to the milling plant in real time so as to minimize post harvest losses.</narrative>
  </description>
